- Updated `POST /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id/query` and the documented `GET /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id/...` endpoints (health, mdm, macadmins, software, encryption_key, recovery_lock_password, certificates, configuration_profiles, activities, activities/upcoming, managed_account_password, reports, reports/:report_id, and scripts) to also accept a host's serial number, UUID, or hostname. A host ID takes priority, followed by serial number, UUID, and hostname.
- BREAKING: Host lookups by identifier no longer match a host's osquery host ID or node key. This applies to `GET /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id`, `POST /api/v1/fleet/translate`, and the hosts targeted by `POST /api/v1/fleet/reports/run_by_identifiers` (`fleetctl query --hosts`).
- Host lookups by identifier, including `POST /api/v1/fleet/translate`, now return the newest host when several hosts share the identifier, instead of the oldest.
- BREAKING: `fleetctl get host`, `fleetctl mdm run-command`, `fleetctl mdm lock`, `fleetctl mdm unlock`, `fleetctl mdm clear-passcode`, `fleetctl mdm wipe`, and `fleetctl run-script` now also accept a host ID, and resolve a host the same way as `GET /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id`: a host ID takes priority, followed by serial number, UUID, and hostname. A number that is a host ID no longer matches another host's serial number, UUID, or hostname.
- BREAKING: Removed the `POST /api/v1/fleet/hosts/identifier/:identifier/query` endpoint. The path now returns 410. Use `POST /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id/query` instead. API-only users granted the removed endpoint are granted `POST /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id/query` instead.
